<!--
    A bike bearing a cog and a bolt: the same leg, in a city whose network
    lends both kinds side by side (SPEC §15).

    The bike is that of ic_bike, at its size and in its place, and the two
    marks take the two corners it leaves empty: the cog on the left flank, the
    bolt on the right. What one pedals alone, and what a motor helps to pedal
    — one on each side of the rider, and nothing between them to read.

    Stacking the two on the left, as this drawing did before, cost the cog its
    teeth: under the bolt it had a radius of 2.30 and read as a dot, and the
    bike had to shrink to give it even that. Given the whole left flank it has
    3.90, with a unit of clear air all round, and the bike is drawn full size
    like the plain and electric ones — which matters, since the welcome page
    shows the three side by side (SPEC §7.9).
-->
